# libpdx-volume — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R53 (design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §2.4 + §9.4, paideia-os
# repo). libpdx-volume is a shared CLIENT-side library, not a standalone
# tool: it performs no `sys_svc_lookup` of its own and binds no ambient
# service at process start. Every public entry point takes a caller-
# supplied capability slot or raw pointer as a plain `u64` argument and
# operates against a KIND surface the CALLER already holds. This file
# therefore declares the KIND surfaces this library's functions are
# TYPED against (so `mkfs.pdxfs` / `mount.pdxfs` / `umount.pdxfs` know
# what to grant themselves before calling in), not a runtime grant the
# loader must satisfy before this library's own code can run.
#
# consumed_kinds (kernel-owned; paideia-os repo):
#
#   KIND_VOLUME            = 0x1A0  (R52, src/kernel/core/cap/kind_volume.pdx)
#     -- vol_kind_mint(dev_cap), vol_kind_narrow(vol_cap, ops_mask).
#        Rights band R_VOL_READ(0x001)/WRITE(0x002)/INVOKE(0x008)/
#        REVOKE(0x010)/REFRESH(0x020)/OBSERVE(0x400), R_VOL_ALL=0x43B.
#        vol_kind_narrow's `ops_mask` parameter is planned (per
#        volume-tooling-ux.md §2.4) to narrow to {mount, query, flush,
#        snapshot} -- none of those four op names exist on
#        KIND_VOLUME's op table yet (kind_volume.pdx currently defines
#        only VOL_OP_QUERY_* + VOL_OP_DEBUG_PRINT, ordinals 0..9); the
#        "mount" op arrives with a future R53 KIND_VOLUME landing this
#        library does not control. See design/architecture.md §5 for
#        the M1 stub's placeholder posture on this gap.
#
#   KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE = 0x1A5  (R53-PREP-001,
#     src/kernel/core/cap/kind_pdxfs_mount_table.pdx)
#     -- mount_table_row_parse(row_ptr, out_ptr) parses the raw 64-byte
#        row layout SECTION 1 of that file defines. At R53-PREP-001 the
#        KIND's own cap-invoke handler has no LIST/READ_ROW op wired
#        (every op refuses INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED), so this library's
#        parser operates on a caller-supplied raw pointer rather than
#        going through a cap-invoke call -- the caller is expected to
#        have already obtained `row_ptr` by some other route (today:
#        none; this is scaffold-ahead-of-the-op-walker, matching the
#        M-PREP posture the kind file itself documents in its SECTION 6
#        header comment). (M2) mount_table_snapshot will need the real
#        LIST op once a future R53 landing wires it.
#
#   KIND_SIG_KEY           = 0x1A3  (R52, per design/filesystem/
#     volume-fs-substrate.md §2.1 sig_key_hash + design/tooling/
#     volume-tooling-ux.md §2.1) -- (M3) pdxb_sign_superblock. Not
#     referenced by any M1 function.
#
#   KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE      = 0x198..0x19F band (R51, osarch-owned) --
#     (M2) vol_kind_mint's `dev_cap` argument narrows a probed
#     KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE into a fresh KIND_VOLUME. Not dereferenced by
#     the M1 stub.
#
# declares_output_schemas: none at M1. Schema registration
# (PdxFsFormatRecord@0.1 / PdxFsMountRecord@0.1 / PdxFsUnmountRecord@0.1)
# is owned by the three CLI tools per design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md
# §7.4; this library supplies the field values those records carry
# (PdxbSuperblockSummary, MountTableRow) but never emits a record onto a
# semantic pipe itself.
#
# M1 landing status (see STATUS.md): every function listed above is a
# scaffold STUB except mount_table_row_parse, which has a real body
# (M1-002) because it operates on a fixed 64-byte layout already frozen
# by R53-PREP-001 -- there is no "M2 real body" gap to defer for that
# one function the way there is for the superblock codec and the
# KIND_VOLUME helpers, which depend on KIND surfaces / wire layouts
# this repo does not own and that have not landed kernel-side yet.
